Z||000018||Formula88||12-13-2001||02:32 PM||||Anyone see the movie "Swordfish" ?<BR>I like his method for dealing with terrorists (not his method of funding, though,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>"They bomb a building, we bomb 10."<P>"They hijack an airplane, we take out an airport."<P>"They kill American tourists, we tactically nuke an entire city."<P>"Someone has got to bring their war to them."<P>I couldn't agree more.  I am not against any one religion or nationality.  But if the cost of the 9-11 attacks was for us to obliterate Afghanistan - totally, completely, and with extreme prejudice - perhaps the next country harboring terrorists will think twice.  <P>Saddam Hussein?  Glass the entire country.<BR>Palestine?  If Arafat doesn't get off the fence, them too.<P>Civilian casualties?  Yes.  But if their death is an example that prevents further terrorist acts, then they didn't die in vain.<BR>Yes, it's extreme.  But as long as it can be gotten away with, people will continue to terrorize.  <P>In WWII, we very nearly obliterated both Germany and Japan, not just the military, or the "bad guys" but the entire country, by the end of the war.  It may take that kind of devastation here.  <P>I will rejoice and dance in the street when I see bin Laden's head on a stake.  ||||reg||8
